{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And he spoke to their heart.</b> Rashi explained that he drew an a fortiori argument on his own: ten lamps could not extinguish one lamp. The meaning is smoke [עשן] of ten lamps, for it is the nature of smoke to extinguish a lamp."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {0 "The comment explains Rashi's analogy: the word עשרה (ten) is read as עשן (smoke), which clarifies why ten lamps would extinguish rather than light a single one."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:34.328805257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}